From 2aed2167f44f8a7ae7bbc93a34a467d00659a014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:22:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] automation replay: a replay refused by a quota wall
 that still holds waits for the new reset

A failed automation turn gets one delayed replay, at the recorded quota reset. When the wall had not
lifted by then (hub chat 20261101_012339_5a8ef0, Nov 17: the replay fired at the 11:09:59Z reset,
Anthropic still answered 429 credits_required and the pool rebooked 12:10:12Z), the replay gave up and
the Kanban notice waited 8.5 h for a manual "resume" although the model served again by 13:06Z.

A replay whose failure is a typed wall with a reset still ahead (within 24 h) is now re-armed at that
reset, at most WALL_REPLAYS_MAX (3) replays in all, for both the turn-failure and the build-failure
(replay_failed_wake) paths. The re-armed replay carries the original deliveries (one note, attempt
number, first failed_at), not a nested note. Any other replay failure still gives up.

Self-heal provider-169ae0ed1f (t_7508ce99d66e4f10).
